The macOS Data volume. macOS mounts Data at /System/Volumes/Data and reaches it through the firmlinks
in the system volume's /usr/share/firmlinks; APFS sets those only for the Data volume of the system
volume's own group. The owner Data volume is on another device:
- on XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX, init's owner Data mount is native_owner_macos_data_prepare: the mount of
  native_owner_data_prepare at /System/Volumes/Data, then each listed firmlink set with
  vnode_setasfirmlink (entries without a source or target are skipped and logged; /private is
  required, as /etc, /var and /tmp resolve through it). The iPadOS function is left unchanged.
- then the OS cryptex view at /System/Volumes/Preboot/Cryptexes/OS (native_cryptex_os_view's binds at the
  macOS path) and, with gpu-addon=1, the GPU addon's plugin over /System/Library/Extensions.
- lookup follows a firmlink source directory on a name cache miss as cache_lookup_path does on a hit.
Requires offline-owner-systemos-mount.patch, zzy-native-gpu-addon-mount.patch and zzyb-native-cryptex-os-view.patch.
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
index 20cda24..095a12b 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -8975,6 +8975,210 @@ done:
 }
